*raises hand* That was me... except I didn't do it on purpose.


> I was playing a wishless/genoless priest on alt.org.  I don't play
> priests often but this one was doing OK despite the game being stingy
> with equipment.  About 8 levels into Gehennom I went down a ladder and
> found myself in a perfectly cleared circle of the maze.  All of the
> walls had been dug out in this circle, and there were no rocks,
> equipment or debris of any kind. Just blank space around the stairs
> where somebody had cast the Light spell and had engraved Elbereth on
> the stairs.

Yup, that was my last gnomish healer who was on a Gehennom Remodelling
Streak. You should've seen the previous levels... not only was a circle
cleared out, entire levels were completely turned into brightly-lit Big
Rooms. Also, I was being a neatnik, and completely picking all loot and
other debris and depositing them in various containers or just burying
them with boulders over pits. (Yes, I was *really* bored. You kinda get
bored in any game that tries to be extinctionist---and I found out after
I died that I wasn't even close to being one.) I believe the E-word was
due to preemptive hogging of the up stairs before a certain master lich
got to it. (I didn't do it just to scare people, honest!)


> So imagine yourself in the middle of the maze in the center of the
> black circle.  Off to the right the maze walls appear again and inside
> are five or six "number 5's" (seen by Warning) wandering around.

Yes, those would include the surviving members of my Gehennom
Remodelling Crew.  :-)


> I finally got the nerve to go in there and found the bones file, but of
> course I have forgotten the name.

That would be Durak, who lived up to his name by getting killed in the
lamest possible way. (The cookie came right after a white dragon. You'd
think I'd learned my lesson by then.)


> He died choking on a fortune cookie and left behind 4 pet purple
> worms, all named creatively and around level 28-30.  I looted the pile
> and tamed his worms and took them along.

Good thing you saw invisible, then. All of the worms were fast and
invisible (zapped with /oSpeed and /oInvis), just so they would gobble
up monsters faster, and have an extra fear factor for monsters that
can't see invis (which is not many at this dungeon depth, admittedly).
Some of the worms had swallowed quite a good number of wraiths, and so
were above the natural max level for purple worms.


> Unfortunately I died the next level because I'd forgotten the Priest
> quest helm doesn't provide magic resistance and an arch-lich got me
> with the finger of death.

NO YOU DID NOT!!!!! There was an MR cloak in the pile, dangit... I
specifically "wasted" a wish on it 'cos another lich (I think it was a
demilich) destroyed my +4 robe with destroy armor. You could've brought
my worms all the way to ascension. ;-)


> So to whoever left the bones level, it was very creative and I
> appreciate the effort you put into creeping me out.  Thank you!
[...]

Now this is funny, 'cos it wasn't intentional at all (choking on a
fortune cookie would be a REALLY lame way to deliberately leave a bones
pile). The circle of cleared walls around the stairs wasn't intentional
either... I had become so bored of the remodelling streak (but was bent
on doing it anyway, for various obsessive reasons) that I had started to
do it in patterns. Usually, I start out with a circle and then gradually
expand it until it covers the entire level, but in this case, I spotted
a shapechanger (lethal to gobble-hungry purple worms) so I teleported
away to take it out before my pets got to it. You'd no doubt have
noticed other areas with cleared out walls, especially near the tomb.

As for the pet names, I've already explained them elsewhere so I won't
repeat it here.

Now, hopefully somebody else will pick up the worms and bring them on.
:-)


